Title

Interfacing Potentiometer with LCD Display

Aim

To display potentiometer values on a 16×2 LCD using Arduino.

Theory

LCD displays are used to show output information. Arduino reads the analog value from the potentiometer and displays it on the LCD.

Components Required
Arduino Uno
16×2 LCD Display
Potentiometer
Jumper Wires
Procedure
Connect LCD pins with Arduino.
Connect potentiometer output to analog pin A0.
Include LCD library.
Upload the program.
Rotate the potentiometer.
Observe values on LCD.
Code
#include <LiquidCrystal.h>

LiquidCrystal lcd(12,11,5,4,3,2);

void setup()
{
  lcd.begin(16,2);
}

void loop()
{
  int value = analogRead(A0);

  lcd.clear();
  lcd.print("Value:");
  lcd.print(value);

  delay(500);
}
Output

LCD displays potentiometer values.

Result

Potentiometer values were successfully displayed on LCD.

Conclusion

Interfacing of potentiometer with LCD was successfully performed.
